b:
Okay, but these are huge spoilers, beginning to end:

Why the story is shit:

* &gt;!The protagonist saves the antagonist's life before she kills him!&lt;

* &gt;!You are forced to play as the antagonist for ~10 hours!&lt;

* &gt;!The main character is on a big revenge tour, kills hundreds of people, but in the final fight with the antagonist, she has a flashback about her loved one, and decides to spare the antagonist's life and both of them just leave on their separate ways!&lt;

* &gt;!During their fight, the antagonist bites off two of the main character's fingers, in one of the final scenes, the main character finds out that her partner left her due to her violent revenge tour, so she decides to play a song on the guitar that her loved one gave her, but she realizes she can't play it due to her missing fingers!&lt;

Why the characters' actions are idiotic:

* &gt;!Even though we had the protagonist and his brother introduced as survivors who don't trust people outside their group, not easily at least, but in the game, after the protagonist saves the antagonist's life, they decide to tell their real names AND CAMP LOCATION to the antagonist and her armed friends in a locked room, they knew them for about 30seconds at this point!&lt;

* &gt;!Turns out that the antagonist just simply kills everyone named "The Protagonist" she doesn't even ask their last name or anything, she just simply kills every human called The Protagonist!&lt;

* &gt;!As I said previously, the majority of the game is about the main character going on a revenge tour, she violently kills tons of people, but just one flashback about her loved one makes her spare the antagonist's life!&lt;

&gt; Are you judging the leaks that only show 1/10 of the game

With the recent leaks, there is about 5 hours of footage online, alongside text leaks from some anonymus reviewers. Hardly 1/10 of the game.

I hope my answer was satisfying.
